cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Census Research Engine"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit and MCP server for extracting American Community Survey
  5-year data from the US Census Bureau API into research-ready files, with
  vintage-safe variable concordance, margins of error for derived estimates,
  constant-dollar conversion with R-CPI-U-RS, and validation against
  Census-published values.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: cafeTechne
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/cafeTechne/Census-Research-Engine"
version: "0.15.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23925301"
# doi: Zenodo concept DOI, added after the first archived release (see CHANGELOG.md "Releasing").
date-released: "2026-11-09"
keywords:
  - American Community Survey
  - US Census Bureau
  - margins of error
  - survey statistics
  - research data
